    ## Research Findings
  - (Filled in below after research.)
  + Recall: yopedia already has "Agent Changelog Delta Analysis" and "AI Coding Agent Failure-Mode Parity" (read each rival changelog entry as a yoyo issue class). I followed that practice. Source: the Claude Code changelog for 2026-10-26 and 10-27 (code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog). Saved to yopedia (job ec14309a).
  + 
  + Each entry below is mapped to where yoyo stands at a7f4b527:
  + - **Write refuses to overwrite a large CLAUDE.md or rules file after seeing only its start.** yoyo has had this since Day 241 (partial_read_guard), plus the truncation retract (813a7289). The never-read overwrite (#1094 item 1) is still an undecided policy in yoyo.
  + - **json/stream-json now escape DEL, C1 controls and Unicode format characters (bidi, zero-width) as \uXXXX inside strings.** yoyo serialises through serde_json, which escapes only control characters below 0x20, quotes and backslashes. So U+202E and zero-width characters reach a JSON consumer raw. CLAUDE.md already names bidi as a known gap in `sanitize_for_display`. This gap is UNPROBED: I did not run a stream-json turn with a bidi character. It is a possible new issue, not a confirmed bug.
  + - **A shell command that reaches its timeout now shows the output so far and says it keeps running in the background.** yoyo shows the output so far (tools.rs:661) and kills the command. Partial parity. The difference is a design choice, not a defect.
  + - **"Background session exit messages no longer promise a restart that isn't coming."** This is the same class as yoyo's #1088/#1086: a surface promising something that the current context can't deliver. That class is live in yoyo as #1086.
  + - **"Per-directory skills found after a Bash cd."** Same class as yoyo #1040 (/cd into a trusted project loads nothing new). Still open.
  + - **"An invalid command name stopped all commands loading; -p printed nothing."** I probed yoyo's equivalent: a SKILL.md with malformed frontmatter (`name: [unclosed`) beside a good one. `yoyo skill list --skills sk` loaded both, falling back to the dir name for the bad one, exit 0. **yoyo is resilient here.** No bug.
  + - Compaction re-asks when the summary is missing: that is yoagent territory. Hook concurrency is capped at 24 per session: yoyo has no equivalent cap and runs hooks serially, as far as I know. Unverified.
  + 
  + **Biggest gaps vs Claude Code (unchanged):** no TUI, no cloud or remote sessions, and no live reload of a project's config on /cd (#1040). Sub-agent spend is still invisible in /cost (#1073).
  + 
  + ## Suggested priorities for the planner (assessment's view, not binding)
  + 1. **#991 items 3, 4a and 4b.** The creator narrowed it 7 days ago with a precise done-when. It sits in prompt/, so it respects the concentration warning. Each item is "fixed with an emission-point test, or measured and recorded unreachable". A null result is an acceptable deliverable, and the plan should say so up front (d203).
  + 2. **#1086: shell usage text in REPL slash syntax.** About 9 verbs are live (find, run, grep, blame, ast, docs, tree, goal / goal set), plus `yoyo help doctor` line 14. This is the dispatch_sub, commands and help_data subsystems. The title should name the class predicate, not an enumerated verb list (d232), or each verb should be probed at plan time (the probe above already did that). `todo` needs its own decision, because todos are session-only.
  + - Avoid main.rs this session (5/10 concentration). That rules #1100 out for now.
